Subject: [PATCH] thermal: mediatek: add calibrated, polled MT7987 LVTS

Base: Linux 6.18.51 (f6388029ea9e2c9e807d73827658738ea131faee).

Combine the E87N 6.12 patches 830/831, preserving their two sensors,
calibration offsets, coefficients and device command sequences. This
baseline uses direct calibration functions, not calibration ops pointers.

The reference DTS provides no LVTS IRQ. Use get_temp-only thermal ops,
require nonzero normal and passive polling delays for associated zones,
and skip IRQ lookup/request. Keep the existing unconditional MONINT=0
initialization; disabling IRQ support must not leave stale enables.
Reject unknown sensor IDs. Also guard the interrupt path against valid
sensors which have no registered thermal zone.

Reject missing/short calibration blobs before either first-word read.
MT7987 has no evidenced default calibration: reject zero/out-of-range
golden temperature and blank sensor words instead of fabricating data.

This provides software-polled sensing and thermal-core critical actions,
not proof of hardware shutdown or CPU throttling. Real temperature
accuracy, sensor coverage, trips and fan response require board tests.

